    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d477">

                <pb facs="0415" n="405" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg405"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.001 Chiang Kai-shek/7–549: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister-Counselor of Embassy in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-05T15:00:00+08:00">July 5, 1949—3 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:53 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 689. President Li Tsung-jen tells me no meeting with Generalissimo has yet
                    been arranged. In view Li’s previous statement that if Generalissimo did not
                    come Canton he and Yen Hsi-shan would visit Generalissimo, it would seem
                    Generalissimo is the reluctant bride.</p>
                <p>Sent Dept Cantel 689, repeated Nanking 462, Shanghai 898.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
